# Battle Targeting System

## Core Principles
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Universal-Targeting-Rules
// - @battle-state-persistence.mdc#Frontend-vs-Backend-Balance

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Movement-Mechanics#Target-Selection
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Network-Effects#Strategic-Impact

1. Proximity is the ONLY targeting factor
2. No type-specific preferences ever
3. Closest valid target is always selected
4. Target changes only when proximity changes

## Stats Reference
// Implementation of:
// - @DigitalBarracksScreen.tsx#BOT_CATEGORIES
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Battalion-Stats

Battalion stats are defined in @DigitalBarracksScreen.tsx and include:
- Guardian: range: 4, speed: 9
- Phreak: range: 9, speed: 7
- Breacher: range: 5, speed: 5

These stats affect HOW battalions engage (range, speed) but NEVER WHO they target.

