// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Pre-Battle#Target-Indicators

### Priority Order
1. Random available node:
   - Neutral nodes within initial restrictions
   - Must follow initial node targeting rules

### Line Restrictions
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Battle-Flow#Pre-Battle-Phase
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Network-Structure#Initial-Node-Control

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Network-Effects#Network-Connectivity
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Network-Display#Line-Visualization

- Initial attack restrictions:
  - Node 0 battalions: Can target nodes 3, 4
  - Node 1 battalions: Can target nodes 3, 4, 5
  - Node 2 battalions: Can target nodes 4, 5
- After initial attack:
  - Can target any node reachable via network lines
  - Must stay on network lines when moving
  - Must reach nodes to change direction

## Target Selection Rules
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Universal-Targeting-Rules
// - @battle-state-persistence.mdc#Frontend-vs-Backend-Balance

### Universal Targeting Priority
// Referenced by:
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Movement-Mechanics#Target-Approach
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Network-Effects#Strategic-Impact

- ALWAYS target nearest available entity:
  - Enemy battalions OR non-captured nodes
  - NO distinction between target types
  - ONLY factor is distance to target
  - Must be reachable via network lines
- Target changes ONLY when:
  - Current target is destroyed/captured
  - A different target becomes closer
  - Current target moves out of reach

## Combat Range
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Battalion-Stats
// - @DigitalBarracksScreen.tsx#BOT_CATEGORIES

### Range Calculation
// Referenced by:
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Attack-Range-Behavior#Range-Requirements
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Effects#Range-Indicators

- Use range values from @DigitalBarracksScreen.tsx
- Calculate from battalion center to target center
- Stop when attack range edge reaches target
- Update position on global 1-second timer

### Attack Positioning
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Movement-Mechanics#Attack-Range-Behavior
// - @battle-state-persistence.mdc#Update-Frequency

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Effects#Position-Feedback
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Network-Effects#Strategic-Impact

- Move to range edge if target beyond range
- Stay in current position if target within range
- Must reach nodes to change movement direction
- Update position only if target moves out of range

## Retargeting Logic
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Universal-Targeting-Rules
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Combat-State-Updates

### Trigger Conditions
// Referenced by:
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Movement-Updates#Retargeting
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Effects#Target-Change

- Current target destroyed
- Node captured
- Target moves out of range
- Better target becomes available (based on proximity)

### Target Acquisition
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Battalion-Combat
// - @battle-state-persistence.mdc#When-to-Persist

- Check if potential target within current range
- If within range, begin attacking immediately
- If beyond range, calculate path via network lines
- Account for required node stops when pathfinding

### Retargeting Priority
// Referenced by:
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Movement-Mechanics#Path-Priority
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Network-Effects#Strategic-Impact

1. Nearest available target, regardless of type:
   - Enemy battalions
   - Non-captured nodes
2. Distance calculation:
   - Measured from battalion center to target center
   - Must be reachable via network lines
   - Must be within attack range

### Retargeting Rules
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Universal-Targeting-Rules
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Combat-State-Updates

- ALWAYS select nearest valid target
- Must be reachable via network lines
- Clear visual indication of new target selection
- Begin attacks immediately if in range

### Retargeting Logging
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Logging-Standards#Battle-Event-Logging
// - @battle-state-persistence.mdc#Development-Strategy

Format: "[Target] {side}.{type}.{battalionId} -> {action}"
Examples:
- "[Target] User.Breacher.5 -> Retargeting"
- "[Target] User.Breacher.5 -> Selected node 7 (nearest)"
- "[Target] User.Breacher.5 -> No valid targets"

