### Combat Flow
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Control-Progress
// - @battle-state-persistence.mdc#When-to-Persist

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Effects#Control-Feedback
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#State-Synchronization#Update-Process

Frontend Flow:
- Target selection (proximity-based only)
- Movement calculation
- Range validation
- Animation triggers

Backend Flow (1s updates):
- Position validation
- Damage calculation
- Health updates
- State persistence

Node Control:
- Apply damage to neutral nodes
- Update control progress for attacking side
- Check capture threshold status
- Handle opposing side's control damage
- Trigger capture state changes

Battalion Combat:
- Calculate total attack: base_offense * battalion_quantity
- Apply defense reduction: damage = total_attack * (1 - target_defense/100)
- Ensure minimum damage of 1 point
- Update target battalion's total health
- Check for battalion destruction
- Update visual feedback and state

### Damage Application
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Damage-Calculation#Node-Control-Damage
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Capture-System#Control-Progress

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Effects#Damage-Feedback
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Attack-Range-Behavior#Combat-Updates

Node Control Damage:
- Track damage contribution to node control
- Account for existing control progress
- Update capture threshold progress
- Trigger state changes on capture
- Synchronize with global timer

Battalion Damage:
- Calculate total attack based on quantity
- Apply percentage-based defense reduction
- Ensure minimum damage of 1
- Update total health (base_health * quantity)
- Track health percentage for visual feedback
- Trigger destruction at 0 total health

## Performance Considerations
### Optimization
- Efficient target validation
- Quick range calculations
- Smooth targeting transitions
- Proper resource management

### Error Handling
- Handle invalid targets
- Manage targeting failures
- Log targeting issues
- Implement fallback logic

## Development Approach
### System Stability
- Preserve working targeting behaviors when making changes
- Test changes in isolation before integration
- Maintain existing targeting priorities and rules
- Document any behavioral changes

### Improvement Process
1. Identify specific targeting issue to address
2. Verify current behavior before making changes
3. Make minimal necessary modifications
4. Validate changes don't break existing functionality
5. Update documentation with new behaviors

### Clarification Requirements
- Seek user input on unclear targeting behaviors
- Verify expected battalion behavior patterns
- Confirm priority changes before implementation
- Document confirmed behavioral requirements

Remember: Targeting must respect network line restrictions and battalion-specific priorities while maintaining system performance. 
